From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bartosz Nitka <niteria@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 11:34:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nvme: apple: take T8132's ANS through a deep sleep

Give T8132's ANS the sleep values T8140's uses. They haven't been traced
on T8132 yet; with them the J713's NVMe comes back from every deep sleep
tested.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Bartosz Nitka <niteria@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit b90d579f08be1d166c5d431a04b66b685c1742a4)
[Dylan: our T8132 entry carried untraced probe values for the same four fields (sleep_probe, the whole endpoint map, SHN normal); they are dropped and Aurora's traced T8140 values kept, as the pick intends.]
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/nvme/host/apple.c | 15 +++++----------
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/nvme/host/apple.c b/drivers/nvme/host/apple.c
index a866bb35d4..5801fc8a83 100644
--- a/drivers/nvme/host/apple.c
+++ b/drivers/nvme/host/apple.c
@@ -3106,18 +3106,13 @@ static const struct apple_nvme_hw apple_nvme_t8132_hw = {
 	.needs_ioq_registers = true,
 	.cold_reset = true,
 	.max_queue_depth = 64,
+	/* T8140's values: T8132's sleep path hasn't been traced. */
+	.sleep_traced = true,
+	.sleep_epmap_last_mask = BIT(0),
+	.sleep_flush_max_nsid = 1,
+	.sleep_shn = NVME_CC_SHN_MASK,
 	/* Explicit flushes are required for writes to survive a reset on J713. */
 	.quirks = NVME_QUIRK_BROKEN_FUA,
-	/*
-	 * Only in a suspend-to-RAM that apple-s2r drives (pm_suspend_via_firmware());
-	 * s2idle is unchanged. SHN: the spec's normal shutdown, as this driver sends at
-	 * final shutdown. Warm restart: the whole endpoint map echoed, RTKit's default.
-	 * Flush: namespace 1, the one Linux mounts. All three are to be measured.
-	 */
-	.sleep_probe = true,
-	.sleep_epmap_last_mask = U32_MAX,
-	.sleep_flush_max_nsid = 1,
-	.sleep_shn = NVME_CC_SHN_NORMAL,
 };
 
 static const struct apple_nvme_hw apple_nvme_t8140_hw = {
